92186414408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "003c5be3-9b52-54de-b5e9-0ebd26752121" :question/math-academy-id "q-181633" :question/problem "$$\nC=[-1,1],\\,D=\\{n<5∣\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nComplete the following reasoning about the sets $C$ and $D$ (given above):\n\nSince $C$ is {{field-1}} and $D$ is {{field-2}}, we have that {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinalities of two sets cannot be equal if one set is finite and the other is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, notice that \n\n- $C$ is infinite (since it's an interval of real numbers), while\n\n- $D=\\{1,2,3,4\\}$ is finite with $|D|=4,$ .\n\nTherefore, $|C|\\ne |D|.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414425 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13fe2373-2094-5193-8e37-541d3a27e5e1" :knowledge-point/title "Using Arithmetic Sequences to Construct a Bijection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aac8f6a6-e103-503e-b60c-4ae836e31f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "injection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414314} {:answer/id #uuid "e3cc3d0c-9795-5e94-8950-9ae9ab501ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bijection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414350} {:answer/id #uuid "f766e16b-635b-50d7-8f78-1858f178dd1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "surjection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3cc3d0c-9795-5e94-8950-9ae9ab501ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bijection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414350} :answer-field/id #uuid "21f7c105-ae47-596c-976d-18a4e6172011" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414374} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23d04bf0-8f36-50a0-9516-83b04d5b4b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|A|=|B|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414248} {:answer/id #uuid "628483b1-828c-53cd-b4ff-2e5fe750fa31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|A|\\ne |B|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23d04bf0-8f36-50a0-9516-83b04d5b4b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|A|=|B|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414248} :answer-field/id #uuid "a45cdd40-c205-5ed5-9ca5-2a96bed1a550" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414392} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c911035-1cc0-517b-9e9b-f5263917d30f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414262} {:answer/id #uuid "60412a78-527a-5223-93a3-8f26684386eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cdot {3}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414272} {:answer/id #uuid "6eb85ad9-dfcd-524e-91b0-c18ecc1548cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2n-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414283} {:answer/id #uuid "8dda814a-1dc7-5c89-af8f-797cfa33b133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2n+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414300} {:answer/id #uuid "ec2d7442-2519-5aa2-874a-3fee1fe9ae64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4n+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6eb85ad9-dfcd-524e-91b0-c18ecc1548cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2n-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414283} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc890179-dc7f-5f57-91d1-20d6fbb68d35" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b75659ad-fe25-5e83-878e-b9945eaf6be7" :question/math-academy-id "q-181659" :question/problem "$$\nA=N,\\,B=\\{-1,1,3,5,…\\}\n$$\n\nComplete the following reasoning about the sets $A$ and $B$ above:\n\nSince the function defined for each $n\\in N$ as\n\n$$\nf:n\\to {{field-1}}\n$$\n\nis a {{field-2}} of $A$ onto $B,$ we have that {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ have the *same cardinality* if there exists a bijection between $A$ and $B.$\n\nNotice that the elements of $B$ form an (infinite) arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =2 \\\\  & =1-(-1) \\\\  & =3-1 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${b}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-1+(n-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-1+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $B$ in set-builder notation as \n\n$$\nB=\\{2n-3∣\\,n\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, consider the function $f:A\\to B$ that maps the underlying sets as follows: \n\n| $A$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $⋯$ | $n$ | $⋯$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $B$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $⋯$ | $2n-3$ | $⋯$ |\n\nIn general, for each $n\\in A,$ we have $f(n)=2n-3\\in B.$\n\nNotice that $f$ is described in such a way that it is bijective. Indeed, it's\n\n- injective since $f(n)\\ne f(m)$ whenever $n\\ne m,$ and\n\n- surjective since each element in $B$ (the second row) has a pre-image in $A$ (the first row).\n\nTherefore, $|A|=|B|,$ i.e., the sets have the same cardinality."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13fe