$f$ is described in such a way that it is bijective. Indeed, it's\n\n- injective since $f(n)\\ne f(m)$ whenever $n\\ne m,$ and\n\n- surjective since each element in $B$ (the second row) has a pre-image in $A$ (the first row).\n\nTherefore, $|A|=|B|,$ i.e., the sets have the same cardinality."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414424 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0445833-499f-577f-8ca7-265f72d24b77" :knowledge-point/title "Using Geometric Sequences to Construct a Bijection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d5712b5-5792-554d-8f40-73fe534ecc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|A|\\ne |B|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414255} {:answer/id #uuid "81741bfd-a764-5fc4-911b-02c9e77b0036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|A|=|B|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81741bfd-a764-5fc4-911b-02c9e77b0036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|A|=|B|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414297} :answer-field/id #uuid "1660089b-aae2-502e-8705-8096b17a3d97" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414372} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0299bb8a-9915-5ed0-b427-9ea16c7bfd20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414229} {:answer/id #uuid "6a7d1b24-9b0d-5df5-a3dd-b9407461dedd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "surjective" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414280} {:answer/id #uuid "d3694270-c310-557a-9b25-b3086212444f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "increasing" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414339}] :answer-field/correct {:a